## a_literal_where_no_function_is_expected
error[Z0205]: `fn(x)` stands where no parameter takes a function
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let f = fn(x) x + 1
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^ a function literal
  |
  = help: a function literal is the argument of a parameter typed `Fn(...)`, as `map(xs, fn(i) i / n)`; a function to call by name is defined at the top level, `fn name(i: Int) -> Float { ... }`

## too_many_parameters
error[Z0205]: `fn(i, j)` has 2 parameters, but `Fn(Int) -> ?` takes 1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:13
  |
1 | map([1, 2], fn(i, j) i + j)
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ 2 parameters
  |
  = help: write one parameter per value the function is given

## too_few_parameters
error[Z0205]: `fn(acc)` has 1 parameter, but `Fn(Int, Int) -> Int` takes 2
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:16
  |
1 | reduce([1, 2], fn(acc) acc, 0)
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^ 1 parameter
  |
  = help: write one parameter per value the function is given

## a_written_type_that_disagrees
error[Z0205]: `i` is declared a Str, but `Fn(Int) -> ?` gives it an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | map([1, 2], fn(i: Str) i)
  |                   ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: leave the type out, and the parameter takes the type the function type gives it

## a_body_of_the_wrong_type
error[Z0205]: the body of `fn(i)` gives an Int, but `Fn(Int) -> Bool` needs a Bool
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:22
  |
1 | filter([1, 2], fn(i) i + 1)
  |                      ^^^^^ an Int
  |
  = help: a function passed as a value matches the parameter types and the return type exactly; write a body of that type

## a_body_of_the_wrong_type_for_reduce
error[Z0205]: the body of `fn(acc, x)` gives a Float, but `Fn(Int, Float) -> Int` needs an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:31
  |
1 | reduce([1.5, 2.5], fn(acc, x) acc * x, 1)
  |                               ^^^^^^^ a Float
  |
  = help: a function passed as a value matches the parameter types and the return type exactly; write a body of that type

## a_parameter_declared_twice
error[Z0405]: `i` is declared twice in `fn(i, i)`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:22
  |
1 | reduce([1, 2], fn(i, i) i, 0)
  |                      ^ the second time
  |
  = help: give each parameter its own name

## a_named_function_of_the_wrong_signature
error[Z0205]: `two` has the signature `Fn(Int, Int) -> Int`, but `Fn(Int) -> ?` is needed here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:13
  |
3 | map([1, 2], two)
  |             ^^^ `Fn(Int, Int) -> Int`
  |
  = help: a function passed as a value matches the parameter types and the return type exactly, defaults ignored; write a function with that signature

## not_a_list
error[Z0401]: `list` of `map` must be a List, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:5
  |
1 | map(3, fn(i) i)
  |     ^ an Int
  |
  = help: `map` goes over the items of a list; `[for ...]` and `seq` make one, and `wages["wage"]` is a column, which `add` goes over

## a_column_is_not_a_list
error[Z0401]: `list` of `map` must be a List, but this is a Column
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:5
  |
2 | map(d["x"], fn(i) i)
  |     ^^^^^^ a Column
  |
  = help: `map` goes over the items of a list; `[for ...]` and `seq` make one, and `wages["wage"]` is a column, which `add` goes over

## an_unknown_argument
error[Z0404]: `map` has no argument `by:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | map([1], fn(i) i, by: 2)
  |                   ^^ not an argument
  |
  = help: usage: `map(list, f)`

## start_missing
error[Z0406]: `reduce` needs `start`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | reduce([1, 2], fn(acc, x) acc + x)
  | ^^^^^^ `start` not given
  |
  = help: usage: `reduce(list, f, start)`

## too_many_arguments
error[Z0407]: `map` takes 2 arguments, but more were given
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | map([1], fn(i) i, 3)
  |                   ^ one too many
  |
  = help: usage: `map(list, f)`

## a_failed_item
error[Z0220]: a failed value cannot be used in a list given as an argument: it failed with Z0207 at line 1: index 5 is outside 1..2
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:5
  |
2 | map([1, k], fn(i) i)
  |     ^^^^^^ a failed value
  |
  = help: test it first with `x.is(Failed)`, or keep it in a list for `report` and `len` to skip with a count (section 5.4)

## na_from_filter
error[Z0203]: `f` of `filter` gave NA where true or false was needed
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:20
  |
1 | filter([1, NA, 3], fn(x) x > 1)
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^ answered NA for an item
  |
  = help: decide the missing case in the function: `!is_missing(x) && x > 0`, or `coalesce(x > 0, false)`

## a_body_that_does_not_check
error[Z0215]: `+` does not apply to text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | map([1, 2], fn(i) i + "a")
  |                   ^^^^^^^ text in arithmetic
  |
  = help: `join` puts texts together and `format` builds text from values (release 0.5.0); a number in text converts with `to(x, Float)`

## a_literal_as_a_statement_in_a_block
error[Z0309]: `fn` is only allowed at the top level of a file
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:5
  |
2 |     fn(i) i
  |     ^^ inside a block
  |
  = help: define the function at the top level, or use a project function from `functions/`
